10(3),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"831–836 (1960); Wai-Kai Chen. On the realization of a (p, s)-digraph with prescribed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degrees. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Journal of the Franklin Institute"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 281(5), 406–422 (1966); Richard P. Anstee.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Properties of a class of (0, 1)-matrix covering problems. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Mathematics"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 41(1),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1–9 (1982),","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"with the vertices ordered by out-degree, non-increasing; the order among equal out-degrees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not change the answer (Annabell Berger, “A note on the characterization of digraphic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequences”, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Mathematics"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 314, 38–41, 2014). With a = the out-degrees and b = the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-degrees in that order, it checks Σ a = Σ b and, for each k,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Σᵢ≤ₖ aᵢ ≤ Σᵢ≤ₖ min(bᵢ, k − 1) + Σᵢ>ₖ min(bᵢ, k)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A negative degree or one of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" or more makes the pair not digraphical."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n): a counting sort, then one pass.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inDegrees.count == outDegrees.count"},{"type":"te